-- title:
--   THEOREM 18 — master faces are basic solutions of system (13)
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal G$ be a finite Abelian group, $g_0\ne0$, and $\pi_0>0$. An inequality $\pi\cdot t\ge\pi_0$ defines a face of the master polyhedron $P(\mathcal G,g_0)$ if and only if $\pi$ is a basic feasible solution of system (13):
--
--   $$\pi(g_0)=\pi_0,\qquad \pi(g)+\pi(g_0-g)=\pi_0\quad(g\ne0,g_0),$$
--   $$\pi(g)+\pi(h)\ge\pi(g+h)\quad(g,h\ne0),\qquad \pi(g)\ge0\quad(g\ne0).$$
--
--   The theorem replaces the infinite integer-point description of faces by a finite system of equations and subadditive inequalities. Both directions of the equivalence are part of the target.
--
--   **Formalization Note** A face is a facet generated by tight integer points. Basicness means that tight row coefficient vectors span the full $|\mathcal G|-1$ variable space. The system includes ordered pairs and $g=h$; $\pi(0)=0$, $\pi_0$ is fixed, and the zero right-hand side is excluded.
-- source:
--   Gomory, Some polyhedra related to combinatorial problems, Linear Algebra Appl. 2 (1969), pp. 481–483, THEOREM 18 and system (13). DOI: 10.1016/0024-3795(69)90017-2

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Gomory69_MasterFaces_BasicFeasible

namespace Gomory69.MasterFaces

/-- Gomory (1969), THEOREM 18, pp. 481–483. -/
theorem theorem_18 {G : Type*} [AddCommGroup G] [Fintype G] [DecidableEq G]
    (g₀ : G) (hg₀ : g₀ ≠ 0) (π : MasterIndex G → ℝ) (π₀ : ℝ)
    (hπ₀ : 0 < π₀) :
    IsFace (masterSupport G) g₀ π π₀ ↔ IsSystem13Basic g₀ π₀ π := by sorry

end Gomory69.MasterFaces
